Overlay patch 0042 (visionOS Phase 01): CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME dispatch flip.
The leetal ios-cmake toolchain sets CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME=visionOS for
PLATFORM=VISIONOS, but this tree (game + LUS) dispatches on
STREQUAL "iOS" everywhere. Flip visionOS -> iOS (+ IOS=1 + GS_VISIONOS=1)
at every point where platform init re-runs — each project() call and the
LUS toolchain include re-derive CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME, so the flip appears
THREE times (reference 0022 pattern, proven through 15 device rounds).
Compilers/sysroot/SDKROOT are already locked by then; only dispatch is
affected. Source-level discriminator stays TARGET_OS_VISION;
GS_VISIONOS gates genuinely-vision-specific CMake deltas (Swift app lib,
no SDL2main, no ENABLE_OPENGL — 0004 rev3 / 0044).

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -2,6 +2,15 @@
 
 # Set the project version and language
 project(Ghostship VERSION 2.1.0 LANGUAGES C CXX ASM)
+
+# GS_IOS (overlay 0042): visionOS builds dispatch through the iOS paths.
+# The leetal toolchain re-derives CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME at every project()/
+# toolchain include, so this flip repeats at each such site.
+if(CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME STREQUAL "visionOS")
+    set(CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME "iOS")
+    set(IOS 1)
+    set(GS_VISIONOS 1)
+endif()
 include(FetchContent)
 
 include(cmake/ghostship-cvars.cmake)
--- a/libultraship/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/libultraship/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -19,6 +19,15 @@
 
